ike that and this process has  to be really fast you need to be really  quick at figuring out uh whether you  need a new chunk or not the duplication  is there is is kind of everywhere as  well  um it's not just in the storage backup  systems  um and actually something that was shown  to be uh at some point uh vulnerability  is uh it happened to users at some point  uh from what I understand is that they  try to upload like a huge file that  would normally need a lot of time to  upload and they would notice that they  would immediately get the message that  it's uploaded so that's kind of a  security vulnerability that I think was  fixed uh at some point  um because it would let you know that  somebody else has the same file  and if you have these little chunks  um then that's sensitive to small edits  of the file as well so  um the duplication is really  um is there's a lot of work on  optimizing the duplication processes  many places  um and actually in this duplication a  string matching algorithm as a string  hashing algorithm is used which is car  Praveen fingerprinting and this is one  of the fastest uh string matching  algorithms uh and part of the reason for  that is that it uses hashing right so  instead of comparing substrings actual  substrings it Compares hashes of sub  substrings  um and but I'm not going to go into more  detail about that you might already be  familiar with carp Raven it's kind of a  randomized really fast string matching  algorithm  so you might be thinking why we love  hash table so much right  um well first of all uh in short it  seems like a kind of a perfect  dictionary and why do I say perfect well  when you look at these other data  structures like arrays and linked lists  and binary search trees hash tables are  the only one that run in constant time  when it comes to lookup insert and  delete  um and so that's where the perfect comes  from however where does the illusion  come from well it's only expected right  so it doesn't 